<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 39,481 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 39,481 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 39,481 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 44,167 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 5,939	    11,368</p>
<p>    Import cargo			33,542	    32,799</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, two ships were expected to sail and 10 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		61,000	 Johar		   5/6</p>
<p>Gas oil		  60,000	 New Tatina	    7/6</p>
<p>Chemicals		 7,650	 Bakri Orbitor	 9/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		 10,000	 Wawasan Courage    10/6</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 30,000	 Ying Song Hu	 31/5</p>
<p>Sulphur		   2,000	 Nova-1		  due</p>
<p>Vegoil		   18,000	 Ariston		 3/6</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
